        <h1>LeetCode 2124: Check if All A's Appears Before All B's (C++)</h1>
        <div class="problem-description">
            <p><strong>Problem:</strong>
                Given a string s consisting of only the characters 'a' and 'b', return true if every 'a'
                appears before every 'b' in the string. Otherwise, return false.
            </p>
            <p><strong>Example:</strong>
                Input: s = "aaabbb"<br>
                Output: true<br>
                Explanation: The 'a's are at indices 0, 1, and 2, while the 'b's are at indices 3, 4, and 5.
                Hence, every 'a' appears before every 'b' and we return true.
            </p>
        </div>
        <div class="code-container">
            <button class="copy-button" onclick="copyCode(this)">Copy Code</button>
            <pre><code class="language-cpp">class Solution {
public:
    bool checkString(string s) {
        bool foundB = false;
        for (char c : s) {
            if (c == 'b') {
                foundB = true;
            } else if (foundB) {
                return false;
            }
        }
        return true;
    }
};</code></pre>
